---
title: "Date Cell Editor"
---

Two date editors cover different value types: `agDateCellEditor` for JavaScript [Date](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date) objects and `agDateStringCellEditor` for ISO [date strings](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String).

## Enabling Date Cell Editor

Edit any of the cells in the grid below to see the Date Cell Editor.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Date Editor" name="date-editor" /%}

Enabled with `agDateCellEditor` (configured with `IDateCellEditorParams`); cell values must be [Date](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date) objects.

```js
columnDefs: [
    {
        cellEditor: 'agDateCellEditor',
        cellEditorParams: {
            min: '2000-01-01',
            max: '2019-12-31',
        }
        // ...other props
    }
]
```

### API Reference

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IDateCellEditorParams" names=["min","max","step","includeTime"] /%}

## Enabling Date as String Cell Editor

Edit any of the cells in the grid below to see the Date as String Cell Editor.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Date as String Editor" name="date-as-string-editor" /%}

Enabled with `agDateStringCellEditor` (configured with `IDateStringCellEditorParams`); works with `string` cell values rather than `Date` objects.

The date format is controlled via [Cell Data Types](./cell-data-types/) and the [Date as String Data Type Definition](./cell-data-types/#date-as-string). The default is `'YYYY-MM-DD'` (or `'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss'` for `dateTimeString`).

```js
columnDefs: [
    {
        cellEditor: 'agDateStringCellEditor',
        cellEditorParams: {
            min: '2000-01-01',
            max: '2019-12-31',
        }
        // ...other props
    }
]
```

### API Reference

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IDateStringCellEditorParams" names=["min","max","step","includeTime"] /%}
